  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `Warning::FirstTraverseLow` (`crates/sim/src/verify/types.rs`) gets the field `tilted: bool` with `#[serde(default)]`. A cache saved before this change still loads, and reads as upright.\n- `operation::first_traverse::judge` (`crates/app/src/operation/first_traverse.rs`) puts a 3+2 verdict into the frame in which the user sets the heights. Generate shifts each height by `h - origin.z` into the tilted frame. The new `in_user_frame` adds `origin.z` back to the two heights and sets `tilted` when the frame is not upright. The sim law does not change.\n- A tilted verdict has a new text. It names the heights that the user set, says that they are measured along the tilted tool axis, and gives the raise. It has no `Z` value and no `X/Y`. The text of an upright verdict does not change.\n- Guide: a troubleshooting entry for the new text (`site/content/guide/reference/troubleshooting.md`), and one paragraph in `site/content/guide/multi-axis/indexed.md` that says what the warning gives after a regenerate.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/2991-tilted-first-traverse-message.md`.\n\n## Readings\n\n`examples/guide-multiaxis.camproj`, `Indexed Face1` (B 20 deg, tilt origin Z 20, Fixed clearance height 30). The operation cache was removed in a scratch copy, so `camcraft-cli process` generated it again:\n\n- Before: `the first rapid (move 0) comes from an unknown X/Y at the clearance height Z10.000, under the stock top at Z11.114 - raise the clearance height above Z11.114`\n- After: `the first rapid (move 0) comes from an unknown position at the clearance height 30.000 mm, under the stock top at 31.114 mm (both measured along the tilted tool axis) - raise the clearance height by at least 1.114 mm`\n\nA clearance height of 31.114 or more passes the law (the local value is then 11.114 or more).\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `first_traverse::a_3_2_plane_reads_the_stock_top_along_its_tool_axis` (app): the verdict gives the typed clearance (25, not the local 5), the corner in the same frame (25.209), `tilted: true`, the new text without `Z` or `X/Y`, and the post refusal with the raise. It fails without the change in `judge` (`tilted` stays false).\n- `verify::first_traverse::tests::a_tilted_verdict_names_the_raise_not_a_z_value` (sim): the full tilted text and a serde round trip.\n- `verify::first_traverse::tests::a_verdict_saved_before_tilted_reads_as_upright` (sim): a cache JSON without `tilted` loads as upright, with the old text.\n- `docs_troubleshooting` (app): the new troubleshooting heading matches the source text.\n\n## Gates\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 109 steps, 0 failed (sim, motion and app suites, with `first_traverse`, `clearance_in_stock`, `wcs_start` and `stale_rapid_law`).\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test docs_troubleshooting`: pass.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main`: the diff reaches 234 heavy steps (199 app, 34 motion). On head 9eee9c59d: 234 steps, 0 failed, wall time 58 min. The 16 known-fail steps (#1950, #2845 and others) are red as expected. `motion heavy: pocket3d_hsm` passes.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- A saved cache keeps its old text until the operation is generated again. The verdict and the held post do not change. I did not change the op stamp salt, because that moves each stamp (`deburr_cache_stamp`, `wire_stamp`, the example projects) for a text change. For the same reason I did not regenerate `examples/guide-multiaxis.camproj`. The decision file records the two choices.\n- No GUI check of the Warnings pane. The pane shows the `Display` text that the tests pin.\n\nChangelog: The first-traverse refusal of a tilted (3+2) operation names the clearance height that the user set, says that the heights are measured along the tilted tool axis, and says how much to raise the clearance height.\n\nBranch made from `upstream/main` at 2ec4ad7e0.\n\nFixes #2991\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
